WEBVTT

﻿1

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:39.415
I am a headhunter and I am the
purest form of salesman alive.


00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:42.418
I sell the American dream.


00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.963
I make money out of thin air,
smoke, whole cloth.


00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:48.340
I stand on the shoulders
of giants,


00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:50.509
the hardest of
hardened salesmen.


00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:54.472
Tin men, bible salesmen,
slum realtors.


00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:57.725
We're a wolf pack of
commissioned phone jockeys


00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:01.604
working 70 hours a week without
a net. You hit, you hit big.


00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:03.647
You blank, and the repo man's
tailgating...


00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:05.524
the minivan
at the grocery store.


00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:09.779
This job is a desk, a phone,
a chair and your ass.


00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:13.949
Good morning, Imperial
Automotive Manufacturing,


00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:15.284
Dottie speaking.


00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:17.536
I am who I say I am.


00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:20.289
Johnny Cobra calling, Dot. Need
the name of your Plant Manager.


00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.753
To give out names of employees.
Nature of your business, sir?


00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:27.713
The nature of my business,
Dottie,


00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:29.673
is that I'm down here
at the Nissan plant


00:01:32.051 --> 00:01:34.845
Because your Quality Department
thinks they can run


00:01:34.887 --> 00:01:38.057
a freightliner full of injection
molded crap down my goddamn
throat!


00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:41.185
The person that you need to
speak to is Mr. Rayburn, I'll...


00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:43.229
First name,
first name, first name.


00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.855
Thomas is his first name.


00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:46.565
- Dottie...
- What?


00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.776
Relax. Take a deep breath.
Pat yourself on the back,


00:01:48.818 --> 00:01:51.320
you're doing one helluva job.


00:01:51.362 --> 00:01:54.448
Uh, Mr... Did you say "Cobra"?


00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.617
Call me Johnny.


00:01:59.829 --> 00:02:03.290
Young, old, play sports, college
boy, what am I dealing with?


00:02:03.332 --> 00:02:05.626
I know Tommy does
play golf a lot.


00:02:05.668 --> 00:02:08.504
He's been working here a couple,
three years, probably...


00:02:08.546 --> 00:02:12.341
Chitchat's over, Dot. Boss
is on my ass. Patch me through.


00:02:14.301 --> 00:02:16.929
Rayburn.


00:02:16.971 --> 00:02:18.305
Dane Jensen,
Blackridge Recruiting.


00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:19.932
Thanks for taking my call.


00:02:19.974 --> 00:02:22.268
Yeah, hold up, hold up, bud.
Lemme save us both some time;


00:02:22.309 --> 00:02:24.854
I'm not lookin' to make
a move right just yet.


00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:27.189
Rough as things are out there,
I'm just happy to have the job


00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:29.567
I got. Now I'm up to my ass
in alligators,


00:02:29.608 --> 00:02:32.403
Sweet. Baby. Jesus.


00:02:32.444 --> 00:02:35.447
I cannot believe my guy
was wrong about you.


00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:39.285
- Scuse me? Your guy? What guy?
- This isn't a random call, Tom.


00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:41.745
I was told by
a confidential source,


00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:45.457
even if your golf game was more
screwed up than a soup sandwich,


00:02:48.419 --> 00:02:51.547
He also told me even though
you've only been at Imperial


00:02:51.589 --> 00:02:53.424
for three years, that
you were bright enough


00:02:53.465 --> 00:02:55.259
to at least listen to what
I was recruiting for


00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:04.560
So. You're a headhunter, huh?


00:03:04.602 --> 00:03:08.314
I am a headhunter.
And a headhunter cometh.


00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:11.525
What's the deal
with this gut, son?


00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:14.695
You need to get some exercise,
buddy, you're starting to look


00:03:14.737 --> 00:03:16.572
like the kind of kid
Willy Wonka'd kick out...


00:03:16.614 --> 00:03:18.032
of the chocolate factory.


00:03:18.073 --> 00:03:19.575
Hands up.


00:03:19.617 --> 00:03:21.702
I dunno... we could
play a little football


00:03:21.744 --> 00:03:24.079
when you get home tonight.
If it's still light out


00:03:24.121 --> 00:03:27.541
and I don't have any calls
to make, we'll see.


00:03:35.633 --> 00:03:38.344
- Good morning.
- Hey, hon.


00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:40.054
Ryan eat breakfast?


00:03:40.095 --> 00:03:43.057
- If you can call it that.
- He likes cereal and it's easy.


00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:46.477
Of course he does, Elise,
what kid doesn't like


00:03:46.518 --> 00:03:48.187
colored marshmallows swimming
in whole milk?


00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.314
Momma.


00:03:53.484 --> 00:03:56.362
I like your hair, Lauren,


00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:58.948
looks good on you.


00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:02.034
The point is, he's a mess.
Shh! Be quiet, he'll hear you!


00:04:02.076 --> 00:04:04.745
Anyway, I made an appointment
for him to see the doctor.


00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:06.705
What the hell for, his weight?


00:04:06.747 --> 00:04:09.959
No! I told you a week ago,
he's tired all the time


00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.335
and those bruises...


00:04:11.377 --> 00:04:13.295
- Bruises?
- Can I have chocolate milk?


00:04:13.337 --> 00:04:16.882
- Sure you can, baby.
- Yeah, just a sec.


00:04:20.636 --> 00:04:22.972
Who's calling you so early?
Just some candidate.


00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:25.641
Pushing sixty and wonders
why he can't find a job.


00:04:25.683 --> 00:04:28.727
Because of his age?
That's awful.


00:04:28.769 --> 00:04:29.687
Okay.


00:04:29.728 --> 00:04:33.399
Gotta go.


00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.234
I was thinking maybe I could
drive into the city,


00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.444
we could get lunch...?


00:04:37.486 --> 00:04:41.490
First of the month, hon,
swamped. Call me! Oh...


00:04:49.832 --> 00:04:53.544
I'm done talking about it!
Either manage Bob to get a deal


00:04:53.585 --> 00:04:55.587
or make the son of a bitch quit
so I don't have to pay...


00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:57.589
unemployment on his lazy ass.


00:04:57.631 --> 00:04:59.883
Ed, how do you propose
I force the man to quit?


00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:01.385
For Christ sake, Wilson,


00:05:01.427 --> 00:05:04.680
have a little fun for a change.


00:05:04.722 --> 00:05:07.850
You know what I love
about this place?


00:05:07.891 --> 00:05:09.226
I'm on pins and needles.


00:05:09.268 --> 00:05:12.354
Ed only cares about
making money.


00:05:12.396 --> 00:05:14.606
Man, woman, black,
white, old or young,


00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:18.277
doesn't matter as long
as you're a producer.


00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.487
Bob, were you not here
this past Saturday or Sunday?


00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:23.449
No, I don't think
anyone was here.


00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.702
- You blanked for three months.
- I got two kids,


00:05:26.744 --> 00:05:28.162
my wife had divorced me,


00:05:28.203 --> 00:05:29.913
I started coming in
on the weekends.


00:05:29.955 --> 00:05:33.125
Ah, wife and two kids, I see.
You're gonna score in October?


00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.419
I'm sure gonna try my best.


00:05:35.461 --> 00:05:39.089
Try? Your attitude is to try?
Bob...


00:05:39.131 --> 00:05:40.466
You know what I hate
about this place?


00:05:40.507 --> 00:05:42.718
Nope.


00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.428
Ed only cares about
making money.


00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:45.846
That's why he tolerates
you and your mouthbreathers.


00:05:45.888 --> 00:05:48.682
My mouthbreathers
make more placements


00:05:48.724 --> 00:05:51.727
and out-produce those Ivy
Leaguers you coddle every month.


00:05:51.769 --> 00:05:55.064
What about an attitude that
says "I'll do whatever it takes",


00:05:55.105 --> 00:05:57.483
"I'll work whatever
hours necessary,


00:05:57.524 --> 00:06:02.905
in order to justify your
financial commitment to me, Ed"?


00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.118
Oh...


00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.705
Bob...


00:06:11.747 --> 00:06:15.334
Are you going to get a deal!!!?


00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.545
Yes! Yes, sir.


00:06:18.587 --> 00:06:22.341
Attaboy, Bob. Now get
the fuck back on the phone.


00:06:30.474 --> 00:06:33.811
Bet the place is full
this weekend.


00:06:33.852 --> 00:06:38.065
But... if and when Bob leaves,


00:06:38.107 --> 00:06:40.025
then keep your ears open.


00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:42.027
If he breaches his non-compete


00:06:42.069 --> 00:06:44.404
and calls just one
of our clients,


00:06:44.446 --> 00:06:46.156
I will sue him so deep
and hard...


00:06:46.198 --> 00:06:48.367
that he, his wide-assed
Junior League wife,


00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:51.411
and their two brats will be
sleeping in a cardboard box


00:06:51.453 --> 00:06:53.872
under the overpass on Whacker.


00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:57.209
There's always someone
that thinks they can hang up


00:06:57.251 --> 00:07:00.045
their own shingle, and skip on
down to the home office


00:07:00.087 --> 00:07:03.215
in their skivvies and make phone
calls while the rug rats frolic


00:07:03.257 --> 00:07:06.552
at their feet. It makes me
want to puke blood.


00:07:06.593 --> 00:07:08.846
In 35 years,


00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:11.765
I have never let anyone
slide on their non-compete.


00:07:16.395 --> 00:07:18.856
I leave for Prague in two days.


00:07:18.897 --> 00:07:20.315
Prague?


00:07:20.357 --> 00:07:22.943
You want her
to tell you where it is?


00:07:22.985 --> 00:07:27.489
I know where Prague is.
Overseas.


00:07:27.531 --> 00:07:31.201
I want to spend more time
away from the place, travel,


00:07:31.243 --> 00:07:34.997
indulge my inner Kerouac.


00:07:35.038 --> 00:07:37.791
Time to finalize that succession
plan that we dance around...


00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:39.251
and never do anything about.


00:07:39.293 --> 00:07:42.087
I won't give up control
immediately,


00:07:42.129 --> 00:07:44.590
but one of you will get the job.


00:07:44.631 --> 00:07:48.969
Whoever takes this last quarter
can move into the empty office


00:07:49.011 --> 00:07:51.722
next to this one.
You'll get off a desk


00:07:51.763 --> 00:07:53.098
and you'll receive overrides...


00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.225
from every recruiter
at Blackridge.


00:07:55.267 --> 00:07:58.020
I'll announce the new General
Manager the first of the year.


00:07:58.061 --> 00:07:59.438
Understood?


00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.899
- One hundred percent, Ed.
- Understood.


00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:05.944
Wilson, beat it.


00:08:22.377 --> 00:08:24.880
- The hell is that?
- Cobra wine.


00:08:24.922 --> 00:08:27.341
Spotted it in a small village
in Vietnam last month,


00:08:27.382 --> 00:08:29.134
thought of you.


00:08:29.176 --> 00:08:31.386
- You're supposed to drink it?
- Don't be such an American.


00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:33.013
Of course you drink it.


00:08:33.055 --> 00:08:36.391
But I'm determined to save
it for a special occasion.


00:08:36.433 --> 00:08:39.228
Maybe the next time I do
something truly remarkable.


00:08:39.269 --> 00:08:40.604
Such as?


00:08:40.646 --> 00:08:42.940
I haven't settled
on that as yet.


00:08:42.981 --> 00:08:45.692
How about a record-
breaking October?


00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:47.611
What makes a person remarkable
is the life they live,


00:08:47.653 --> 00:08:49.071
not the money they make.


00:08:49.112 --> 00:08:51.031
Spoken like a man
with a lot of money.


00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:55.786
I may never uncork that wine.


00:08:55.827 --> 00:08:58.455
Ryan...


00:08:58.497 --> 00:09:00.999
Ryan, wake up, pal.


00:09:01.041 --> 00:09:04.419
- What time is it?
- 6:30. Come on.


00:09:04.461 --> 00:09:07.297
Let's get some roadwork in
before school.


00:09:07.339 --> 00:09:08.840
Roadwork?


00:09:13.679 --> 00:09:16.556
Dad! I need to rest.


00:09:16.598 --> 00:09:19.268
Why don't I just carry you?


00:09:19.309 --> 00:09:22.938
- I'm walking.
- You're jogging.


00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.190
Morning, ladies!


00:09:27.734 --> 00:09:31.280
Alright.


00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:34.157
Let's just walk.


00:09:34.199 --> 00:09:37.035
Why don't we go
to Catholic school?


00:09:38.954 --> 00:09:41.873
We're lapsed Catholics.


00:09:41.915 --> 00:09:43.250
The good Lord wants us...


00:09:43.292 --> 00:09:45.294
to spend Sunday mornings
at Cracker Barrel.


00:09:45.335 --> 00:09:47.713
I'm with the Lord.


00:09:49.631 --> 00:09:51.591
How come Lauren
doesn't have to jog?


00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:54.052
'Cause Lauren
doesn't have to lose weight.


00:09:55.971 --> 00:09:58.598
First step in solving a problem
is recognizing it, buddy.


00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.101
Did you and Grandpa go jogging
when you were a kid


00:10:01.143 --> 00:10:04.479
in St. Louis?
No, not hardly.


00:10:04.521 --> 00:10:05.939
He went to work when
it was dark,


00:10:05.981 --> 00:10:07.065
came home when it was dark.


00:10:07.107 --> 00:10:09.401
Wasn't much fun, was he?


00:10:09.443 --> 00:10:12.112
Eh, he did the job.


00:10:12.154 --> 00:10:16.533
"Kinfe," "Sizhong," "Deepak"...


00:10:16.575 --> 00:10:19.244
Don't get me going on the
red dots.


00:10:19.286 --> 00:10:20.787
Here's an invoice
begging to be sent.


00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:24.124
"Ping." Interview
a Chinese engineer yet?


00:10:24.166 --> 00:10:26.626
Treat yourself. It's like having
a conversation in the dark...


00:10:26.668 --> 00:10:28.503
with Astro from the Jetsons.


00:10:28.545 --> 00:10:31.256
Look, Sumner,


00:10:31.298 --> 00:10:32.758
I should have spent more time
with you, okay.


00:10:32.799 --> 00:10:34.134
My fault. Let's start over.


00:10:34.176 --> 00:10:37.179
We are the "Dixie Mafia."
Okay, Dixie.


00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.473
The South. You know,
state's rights, NASCAR,


00:10:39.514 --> 00:10:41.683
closeted atheists,
poor spellers.


00:10:41.725 --> 00:10:43.101
I'm not an idiot,
Mr. Jensen.


00:10:43.143 --> 00:10:45.979
Okay. Role-play with me,
alright.


00:10:46.021 --> 00:10:48.106
I'm a client from Hattiesburg,
Mississippi...


00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:49.691
and I'm looking for
a process engineer.


00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:53.779
So go on, pitch me
one of your PhD's.


00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.698
Ahem! Ring! Ring!


00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:00.035
Darrel Waltrip here!
Uh, yes, Mr. Waltrip?


00:11:00.077 --> 00:11:02.704
Darrel, son.
What can I do you for?


00:11:02.746 --> 00:11:04.206
Well, Darrel,
I'm calling about your...


00:11:04.247 --> 00:11:06.750
Who the hell is this?


00:11:06.792 --> 00:11:08.043
Sumner, Sumner Firestone
from Blackridge Recruiting.


00:11:08.085 --> 00:11:09.378
Spit it out, I'm a busy man!


00:11:09.419 --> 00:11:12.881
Uh... Well, I've got
a guy, he's uh,


00:11:12.923 --> 00:11:15.258
for your open engineering
position I mean,


00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.636
he's got two degrees in
Mechanical Engineering,


00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:19.179
experience reducing waste
in the plants.


00:11:19.221 --> 00:11:20.889
Sounds stronger than puppy's
breath.


00:11:20.931 --> 00:11:21.848
Now, when can he get down here?


00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:25.936
- Well, he can be there Friday?
- You asking me or telling me?


00:11:25.977 --> 00:11:27.604
I'm telling you.
He'll be there Friday.


00:11:27.646 --> 00:11:30.190
Friday it is! By the by,


00:11:30.232 --> 00:11:33.151
he wouldn't happen to have
one of those PhD's, would he?


00:11:33.193 --> 00:11:34.611
As a matter of fact, he does.


00:11:34.653 --> 00:11:37.364
Perfect! Better'n
a new set of snow tires!


00:11:37.406 --> 00:11:40.033
Now, what's his name?


00:11:40.075 --> 00:11:43.328
Mohammed Al Far...


00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.498
Your sleepercell starter kits


00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:50.794
are unemployable
south of the grit-line!


00:11:55.799 --> 00:11:59.511
Alright. Cowboy up, sunshine.


00:11:59.553 --> 00:12:03.181
Use this guy. Lou Wheeler.
Bachelor's


00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:05.725
in Mechanical Engineering,
Six Sigma experience,


00:12:05.767 --> 00:12:07.561
and an age-vague voice.


00:12:07.602 --> 00:12:10.313
- "Age-vague"?
- Yeah. He's 59,


00:12:10.355 --> 00:12:12.941
sounds like he's 39,
and refuses to change the dates


00:12:12.983 --> 00:12:14.734
on his resume,
and is unemployable.


00:12:14.776 --> 00:12:16.736
Why unemployable?


00:12:16.778 --> 00:12:20.991
He's 59 and refuses to lie
about it. God, you and my wife.


00:12:21.032 --> 00:12:23.785
Okay... So why do I want him?


00:12:23.827 --> 00:12:26.538
Because we will


00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:29.207
take 15 years off Lou's resume.


00:12:29.249 --> 00:12:30.542
Right, but once he goes
in for the interview,


00:12:30.584 --> 00:12:31.626
they'll just see how
old he is, I mean,


00:12:31.668 --> 00:12:33.545
what's the point?


00:12:33.587 --> 00:12:34.796
We don't send him
on an interview.


00:12:34.838 --> 00:12:37.632
Lou's what you call
a Tracer Bullet.


00:12:37.674 --> 00:12:40.135
A tracer bullet, you know?


00:12:40.177 --> 00:12:41.261
A round that lights up so you
know where to fire...


00:12:41.303 --> 00:12:43.096
the rest of the real bullets.


00:12:43.138 --> 00:12:45.390
I know what a tracer bullet
is, I just don't understand...


00:12:45.432 --> 00:12:46.975
"Relatively Young Lou"


00:12:47.017 --> 00:12:48.727
is a sure-fire bet for a phone
interview, okay?


00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:51.521
But once he's off the line
with a paying customer,


00:12:51.563 --> 00:12:54.274
you bleed "Actually Old Lou"
for information.


00:12:54.316 --> 00:12:56.234
Like, "What projects are they
working on?"


00:12:56.276 --> 00:12:58.487
"What specifically
did they ask you?"


00:12:58.528 --> 00:12:59.946
And you give that information...


00:12:59.988 --> 00:13:01.656
to your placeable candidates
to prepare them.


00:13:01.698 --> 00:13:04.326
I don't know...


00:13:04.367 --> 00:13:07.078
We're headhunters, Sumner.


00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.915
In an economic shit storm.


00:13:09.956 --> 00:13:11.458
Now I can teach you
how to count cards,


00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.751
but I can't make you do it.


00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:14.586
So you either
reach deep inside


00:13:14.628 --> 00:13:16.922
and find that small
dark part of yourself


00:13:16.963 --> 00:13:19.883
that's predatory...
Or there's the door.


00:13:24.387 --> 00:13:26.473
Alright.


00:13:26.515 --> 00:13:29.935
Try giving yourself a desk name,
something tough, visual.


00:13:29.976 --> 00:13:33.021
Watch Wall Street,
Godfathers 1 and 2, not 3.


00:13:33.063 --> 00:13:35.440
Go on, get your phone,
listen in.


00:13:39.277 --> 00:13:42.739
Bernadine?


00:13:42.781 --> 00:13:45.325
Hey, it's Dane.


00:13:45.367 --> 00:13:48.495
How are you, dear?
Is Lou around?


